# the argument of kant-practical-2.md as claude-opus-5-5 read it: check that it says what the text says
atom	emp	the knowledge of happiness rests on mere empirical data
atom	var	every man's judgement on happiness depends on his particular, very variable point of view
atom	universal	the principle of happiness can supply universal rules that must hold good always and necessarily
atom	law	the principle of happiness can found practical laws, laws of the will
atom	object_found	an object of choice is the foundation of the rule and must precede it
atom	exp	the rule refers to nothing but what is felt, so it refers to experience and is founded on it
atom	endless	the variety of judgement is endless
atom	same_all	the principle prescribes the same practical rules to all rational beings
